-- title:
--   Reducedness of a closed fibre from its adic completions
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ be a commutative local ring, with residue field $\kappa(A) =$ `ResidueField A`, and let $C$ be a commutative Noetherian ring equipped with an $A$-algebra structure. Write $K = \mathfrak m_A C$ for the ideal `(maximalIdeal A).map (algebraMap A C)` of $C$ generated by the image of the maximal ideal of $A$. Assume that for every ideal $x$ of $C$ which is maximal and satisfies $K \le x$, the ring $\kappa(A) \otimes_A \widehat{C}_x$ is reduced, where $\widehat{C}_x =$ `AdicCompletion x C` denotes the $x$-adic completion of $C$. The conclusion is that $\kappa(A) \otimes_A C$ is reduced, i.e. has no nonzero nilpotent elements. No finiteness or flatness assumption on $C$ over $A$ is imposed beyond $C$ being Noetherian as a ring, and only the closed points of the fibre, namely the maximal ideals of $C$ containing $K$, enter the hypothesis.
--
--   This is the local-to-global step passing from reducedness of the completed local rings of the fibre over the closed point of $\operatorname{Spec} A$ to reducedness of that fibre itself. It is applied in the study of the full-level modular curve moduli rings, to deduce that the special fibre of each component of the moduli ring is reduced from local computations at the supersingular and ordinary closed points.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_IsReduced_tensorProduct_residueField_of_forall_isMaximal_adicCompletion.lean

import Mathlib

